+// Every descriptor in the agb_flash_* tables describes the 1 Mbit chip, so
+// this has to keep matching their romSize when a 64-bit build grows the
+// emulated flash past 1 Mbit -- otherwise the bank-switching branches in
+// agb_flash.c silently stop being taken. Bank switching is GBA-only code and a
+// GBA build is always 32-bit, so there it still sees exactly two 16-sector
+// banks, unchanged.
+#define FLASH_ROM_SIZE_1M FLASH_ROM_SIZE // 1 megabit ROM
 
